meta {
  name: Slack - events (url_verification)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/slack/events
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "url_verification",
    "challenge": "challenge-demo"
  }
}

tests {
  test("unsigned requests are refused (or 404 without Slack config)", function() {
    expect([403, 404]).to.include(res.status);
  });
}

docs {
  Slack Events API endpoint. Every request must carry Slack's v0 signature
  (x-slack-signature, x-slack-request-timestamp), so this unsigned request is refused:
  403 with Slack configured, 404 without. Signed by Slack, it answers url_verification
  with { challenge } and turns a person's reply in a handoff thread into a message to the
  visitor. Each event_id is delivered once: a redelivery is ack'd and ignored, and a
  delivery that fails answers 500 so Slack retries it.
}
